UPDATE companies SET description='Alkar-RapidPak, Inc. is headquartered in Lodi, Wisconsin, and traces its origins to the 1950s. The company operates as a division of Middleby Food Processing and Packaging, a global portfolio of food production technology brands.

The company custom engineers batch and continuous cooking and chilling equipment for protein and alternative protein processors worldwide. Its product line includes batch ovens with capacities from 500 to 50,000 pounds, offering direct or indirect gas heat, steam coil, hot oil, high-temperature, BBQ, fermentation, and cold smoking configurations. Continuous processing systems handle up to 10,000 pounds per hour with automated loading and unloading. Chillers and the TurboChef — described as the only industrial oven combining microwave, convection, and steam heating — round out the portfolio. To date, Alkar has installed nearly 400 continuous systems and 6,000 batch units globally.

Alkar serves meat, poultry, alternative protein, pet food, fish, and snack processors.

The company emphasizes process flexibility, product consistency, and automation to lower operating costs. Its differentiation rests on custom engineering that spans scientific advice, process development, plant layout, and equipment design, backed by a support network that the company says has driven its position in the meat and protein thermal processing segment.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom engineering of batch cooking systems", "Custom engineering of continuous cooking systems", "Custom engineering of chilling systems", "Thermal processing (cooking, smoking, chilling, pasteurization)", "Process development and optimization", "Plant layout and design", "Automation integration", "Batch oven manufacturing (gas, steam, hot oil, high-temp, BBQ, fermentation, cold smoking)", "Continuous processing systems (up to 10,000 lbs/hr)", "Chiller manufacturing", "Microwave/convection heating (TurboChef)", "Equipment installation and support"], "industries": ["Meat processing", "Poultry processing", "Alternative protein processing", "Pet food processing", "Fish processing", "Snack food processing"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["TurboChef by Alkar (microwave and convection heating industrial oven)", "Batch ovens", "Continuous processing systems", "Chillers"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Only industrial oven worldwide with microwave, convection & steam heating (TurboChef)", "Nearly 400 continuous systems and 6,000 batch units installed globally", "Batch systems from 500 to 50,000 lbs capacity with multiple heating options", "Continuous processing up to 10,000 lbs/hr with automated loading/unloading", "Custom engineering from process development to plant layout"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Lodi, Wisconsin -> db", "Founded in 1950s -> /", "Division of Middleby Food Processing and Packaging -> /about-us", "Custom engineers batch and continuous cooking and chilling equipment -> /", "Nearly 400 continuous systems and 6,000 batch units installed -> /", "Batch systems 500 to 50,000 lbs capacity -> /about-us", "Continuous processing up to 10,000 lbs/hr -> /", "TurboChef microwave/convection oven -> /about-us", "Industries: meat, poultry, alternative protein, pet food, fish, snacks -> /", "Process development, plant layout, custom equipment design -> /", "Only industrial oven with microwave, convection & steam heating -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "ALKAR custom engineers batch and continuous cooking and chilling equipment for processors all over the world.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='alkar-rapidpak-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='All About Electronics operates from Lyndonville, Vermont, where owner Marc Plourde has provided on-site and drop-off electronics service across a 100-mile radius of Littleton for more than a decade.

The company focuses on repair and support for consumer and small-business electronics. Services span computer and laptop repair, virus removal, data recovery and backup, screen replacement for phones and tablets, soldering of power jacks and motherboards, and repair of televisions and video-game consoles. It also sells refurbished systems starting at $99, builds custom desktops, offers custom laptop painting, and provides server installation and networking support. Loaner computers are available while devices are in the shop, and emergency service runs around the clock.

