UPDATE companies SET description='All-Type Welding and Fabrication, Inc. was founded in 1987 and operates a 34,000-square-foot facility in Glenwillow, Ohio, a suburb of Cleveland. The company has served thousands of customers over more than three decades with custom metal fabrication and welding services.

The shop provides precision metal fabrication, laser cutting, welding, powder coating, prototyping, assembly, and inspection services. Its laser cutting machines handle sheets up to 60 by 120 inches and one inch thick. In-house engineering supports design for manufacturability, and rapid prototyping via 3D printing delivers parts in as little as same-day to five days. Equipment includes a Fronius TPS 320i MIG welder, a TECNA 20 KVA rocker arm spot welder, a Kaeser AS20 compressor, and a Trumpf TruMark Station 300 laser etcher.

Customers span original equipment manufacturers, food equipment, pharmaceutical, material handling, aerospace, military and defense, transportation, power distribution, fuel cell, and construction equipment sectors. Case studies highlight work for an Ohio brewery and a construction equipment supplier.

The company emphasizes that its engineers all began as skilled welders, giving them practical insight into weld behavior across difficult metals such as Inconel, various aluminums, and stainless steels. It holds ISO 9001:2015 certification and qualifies to MIL-STD-1595A, MIL-STD-2219A, and AWS D1.1, D1.2, D1.6, and D17.1 welding specifications.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','MIL-STD-1595A','MIL-STD-2219A','AWS D1.1','AWS D1.2','AWS D1.6','AWS D17.1']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Engineering services", "Laser cutting (up to 60x120 in, 1 in thick)", "Precision metal fabrication", "Powder coating", "MIG welding", "Spot welding", "Laser etching", "3D printing (rapid prototyping)", "Inspection (ISO 9001, MIL-STD, AWS)", "Assembly", "Design for manufacturability"], "industries": ["Foodservice", "Aerospace", "OEM", "Pharmaceutical", "Military & Defense", "Material Handling", "Transportation", "Power Distribution", "Fuel Cell", "Construction Equipment", "Brewery"], "materials": ["Stainless steel (various grades)", "Aluminum (various grades)", "Carbon steel", "Inconel", "Copper", "Brass", "Bronze", "Difficult-to-work-with metals"], "equipment": ["Fronius TPS 320i MIG welding machine", "TECNA 20 KVA rocker arm spot welder", "Kaeser AS20 compressor", "Trumpf TruMark Station 300 laser etcher", "3D printer (rapid prototyping)", "Laser cutting machines (60x120 in capacity)"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Same-day to five days for prototyping depending on complexity", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Engineers started careers as skilled welders", "In-house engineering and prototyping with same-day to five-day turnaround", "Expertise in difficult-to-weld metals (Inconel, various aluminums, stainless steels)", "ISO 9001:2015 certified with MIL-STD and AWS welding specifications", "Full-service 34,000 sq ft facility with laser cutting up to 60x120 inches"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1987 -> /about-us", "34,000 sq ft facility in Glenwillow, Ohio -> /about-us", "Laser cutting capacity 60x120 in, 1 in thick -> /", "Prototyping turnaround same-day to 5 days -> /", "Equipment: Fronius TPS 320i, TECNA 20 KVA, Kaeser AS20, Trumpf TruMark Station 300, 3D printer -> /about-us", "Certifications: ISO 9001:2015, MIL-STD-1595A, MIL-STD-2219A, AWS D1.1, D1.2, D1.6, D17.1 -> /about-us", "Materials: stainless steel, aluminum, carbon steel, Inconel, copper, brass, bronze -> /", "Industries: Foodservice, Aerospace, OEM, Pharmaceutical, Military & Defense, Material Handling, Transportation, Power Distribution, Fuel Cell, Construction Equipment, Brewery -> /, /about-us", "Engineers started as skilled welders -> /about-us", "ISO 9001:2015 SOP mentioned -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "All-Type Welding and Fabrication, Inc. has provided comprehensive precision metal fabrication services since 1987.", "founded_year": "1987", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='all-type-welding-and-fabrication' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Alliance Auto Body Parts operates from Houston, Texas, where it has supplied new replacement auto body parts for over 20 years. The company runs two locations in the city, a structure it says allows greater convenience and faster delivery for customers across the greater Houston area.

The business stocks a broad line of collision repair parts including bumpers, fenders, hoods, fans, grilles, valances, cooling products and lighting products. It serves both the professional collision repair trade and the general public, and emphasizes its willingness to arrange buy-outs and special orders for hard-to-find items.

Customers include independent repair shops, national auto sales companies, and individual vehicle owners. Testimonials on the company''s site reference a parts manager at a national auto sales firm and a shop owner in Cypress, Texas, illustrating a client base that spans wholesale and retail channels.

Alliance Auto Body Parts positions itself on accurate, friendly service, competitive pricing and faster delivery enabled by its dual-location network. The company also highlights its practice of going the extra mile to source special orders and buy-outs as a key reason customers return.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Auto body parts supply", "Cooling products supply", "Lighting products supply", "Special order fulfillment", "Buy-out fulfillment"], "industries": ["Collision repair", "Automotive aftermarket", "Auto sales"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Two Houston locations for faster delivery", "Accurate, friendly service", "Competitive pricing", "Buy-outs and special orders for unique needs", "Broad product line covering most car brands"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Houston, Texas -> db", "Business type: supplier of new replacement auto body parts -> /about", "Years in business: over 20 years -> /about", "Two locations in Houston -> /about", "Product lines: bumpers, fenders, hoods, fans, grilles, valances, cooling products, lighting products -> /", "Industries served: collision repair industry, general public -> /", "Customer examples: national auto sales company, shop in Cypress, Texas -> /about", "Differentiators: accurate friendly service, competitive pricing, faster delivery -> /", "Special orders and buy-outs -> /", "Website: http://www.allianceauto.com/ -> db"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "We are the leading supplier of new replacement auto body parts in the greater Houston area.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='alliance-auto-body-parts' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Alliance Cable & Wire Harness, headquartered in Lindon, Utah, was founded in 1936. The company operates as a boutique manufacturer of custom wire harnesses and cable assemblies, led by an executive team that includes President and CEO Cole Matson, Vice Presidents of Engineering Edd Todd and Sergio Martinez, and Board Advisor Chad London, who brings 35 years of industry experience.

The company provides end-to-end services from design and rapid prototyping through turnkey assembly, overmolding, kitting, drop shipping, and 100% functional testing. Its facility runs a high-mix, low-to-medium volume operation equipped with vertical injection molding machines, Komax cut-strip-crimp systems, ultrasonic splicers, automated solder lines, and in-house 3D printing for fixture development.

Alliance serves customers in oil and gas, robotics and sensors, solar photovoltaics, transportation, audio and video, electronics, instrumentation, and medical sectors. The firm notes long-standing relationships with Fortune 500 manufacturers and supplies businesses across the United States and Canada.

Differentiators cited by the company include vendor-managed inventory and consignment programs, quick-turn prototyping with stocked components, on-site design engineering, and after-market support that extends beyond a decade for obsolete products.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001','ISO 14001','UL 508A']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom wire harness design and engineering", "Rapid prototyping", "Turnkey cable assembly", "Overmolding (rubber/plastic encapsulation)", "Kitting and drop shipping", "Testing and design validation (100% functional test)", "R&D: material research, process innovation, QC, environmental compliance", "Ultrasonic splicing (TelSonic)", "Splice pressing (TE)", "Crimping (automated applicators and hand crimpers)", "Harness testing (Dynalab)", "Vacuum oven processing", "3D printing (Formlabs)", "Automated solder lines", "Automated RJ45 termination", "Vertical injection molding", "Crimp press (Molex, TE, Mecal)", "Komax cut, strip, seal, crimp with CFA", "Komax cut and strip with inkjet marking", "Delta Sigma projection harness boards", "Cobra braiding", "Hot stamping", "Zuken harness builder software", "Full design service"], "industries": ["Oil & Gas", "Robotics & Sensor", "Solar & Photovoltaic (PV)", "Transportation", "Audio & Video", "Electronics", "Instrumentation", "Medical"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["TELSONIC ULTRASONIC SPLICER", "TE SPLICE PRESS", "100+ CRIMP APPLICATORS", "ZUKEN HARNESS BUILDER", "COBRA BRAIDER", "HOT STAMPING", "100+ HAND CRIMPERS", "DYNALAB HARNESS TESTER", "VACUUM OVENS", "3 FORMLABS 3D PRINTERS", "2 AUTOMATED SOLDER LINES", "AUTOMATED RJ45 LINE", "3 VERTICAL INJECTION MOLDING MACHINES", "20+ CRIMP PRESS (MOLEX, TE, MECAL)", "5 KOMAX CUT, STRIP, SEAL, CRIMP MACHINES WITH CFA", "4 KOMAX CUT AND STRIP LINES WITH INKJET", "DELTA SIGMA PROJECTION HARNESS BOARDS"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Vendor-managed inventory (VMI) and customer consignment programs", "Quick-turn prototyping with stocked wire and components", "On-site design engineering and manufacturing", "100% functional and quality testing on every assembly", "After-market support for ten-plus years on legacy products"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1936 -> db", "Headquarters Lindon, Utah -> db", "ISO 9001 certification -> db", "UL508A, ISO 14001 certifications -> /", "Industries served: Oil & Gas, Robotics & Sensor, Solar & Photovoltaic, Transportation, Audio & Video, Electronics, Instrumentation, Medical -> /", "Equipment: TelSonic ultrasonic splicer, TE splice press, 100+ crimp applicators, Zuken harness builder, Cobra braider, hot stamping, 100+ hand crimpers, Dynalab harness tester, vacuum ovens, 3 Formlabs 3D printers, 2 automated solder lines, automated RJ45 line, 3 vertical injection molding machines, 20+ crimp presses (Molex, TE, Mecal), 5 Komax cut/strip/seal/crimp with CFA, 4 Komax cut/strip with inkjet, Delta Sigma projection harness boards -> /capabilities", "Executive team: Chad London (Board Advisor), Edd Todd (VP Engineering), Cole Matson (President/CEO), Sergio Martinez (VP Engineering) -> /about-us", "Capabilities: rapid prototyping, turnkey assembly, overmolding, kitting/drop shipping, testing/design validation, R&D -> /services", "Boutique manufacturer, high-mix low-volume, NPD speed to market -> /about-us", "After-market support over a decade -> /", "VMI programs, customer consignment programs -> /", "Drop-in orders with stocked parts -> /", "100% functionality and quality testing -> /", "Long-term raw material and finished goods storage -> /", "Engineering and technical support -> /", "Full design service -> /", "Serves customers across United States and Canada -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "At Alliance Cable & Wire Harness, we specialize in design, development, and manufacturing of custom wire harnesses", "founded_year": "1936", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='alliance-cable-and-wire-harness' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Alloy Welding and Manufacturing Co., Inc. was founded in 1937 by Delphis “Del” Frechette in Bristol, Connecticut. The company began as a job shop producing fabricated metal parts and welding repairs for local industry, with Del inventing and building much of his original equipment. After surviving the 1955 flood, the business relocated to its current 14,000-square-foot facility Now in its third generation under Darren Frechette, who took over in 2005, the company remains family-owned.

The shop provides metal fabrication, welding, and cutting services including GTAW, GMAW, and SMAW welding, CNC water jet cutting, hand-held laser welding, and portable on-site welding. It also offers metal sales and custom design with project management. The facility houses a CNC water jet and handheld laser welder for thin materials such as stainless steel and titanium, and operates mobile welding trucks for field repairs.

Customers span industrial manufacturers, military, construction, medical, and high-tech sectors, as well as schools, governments, hospitals, apartment complexes, general contractors, and individuals throughout central Connecticut.

