UPDATE companies SET description='Altek Electronics operates from Torrington, Connecticut, where Stephen Altschuler founded the company in 1972 after a career in quality assurance and computer systems.

The company provides full-spectrum electronics manufacturing services from its Connecticut facility, employing 130-plus people. Core processes include surface-mount and through-hole PCB assembly, BGA and leadless device placement, selective and wave soldering, conformal coating (with a PVA6000 system and IR2000 curing oven), wire and cable harness fabrication, box build and system integration, and functional test including high-voltage soldering. Engineering support covers design for manufacturability, component obsolescence management, and traceability.

Altek serves original equipment manufacturers in medical devices, aerospace, defense, telecommunications, industrial/commercial equipment, and transportation. The firm highlights its early adoption of AS9100 (certified to the “D” level in 2017) for aerospace work and ISO 13485 for medical assemblies, alongside IATF 16949 for automotive-related programs.

Altschuler established the company on a culture of customer satisfaction, on-time bill payment, and a reputation for reliability. Leadership states they aim to deliver the highest quality at the most competitive price without compromising core beliefs, emphasizing integrated box build to reduce hand-offs and early manufacturing involvement to avoid prototype-to-production pitfalls.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001','ISO 13485','IATF 16949','RoHS','ITAR']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["SMT Assembly", "Through Hole Assembly", "BGA Placement", "Leadless Device Placement", "Selective Soldering", "Wave Soldering", "High Voltage Soldering", "Conformal Coating (PVA6000/IR2000)", "Wire & Cable Harness Assembly", "Box Build & System Integration", "Functional Test", "Component Engineering", "Design for Manufacturability (DFM) Feedback", "Obsolescence Management", "Traceability & Product Identification", "PCB Conformal Coating and Potting", "3D Printing (MakerBot Extrusion)"], "industries": ["Medical Devices", "Aerospace", "Defense", "Telecommunications", "Industrial/Commercial", "Transportation"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["PVA6000 Conformal Coating Machine", "IR2000 Curing Oven", "MakerBot 3D Extrusion Printer", "ERSA Versaflow 3/66", "Contact Systems CS-400 Component Locators", "Optical Control OC Scan CCX.3 Component Counter", "Barcodes Part Marking Barcode Reader System"], "volume": "Prototype to production", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["ITAR registered for defense work", "Prototype-to-production scaling under one roof", "Integrated box build reduces hand-offs", "Component engineering and obsolescence management"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1972 by Stephen Altschuler -> / (home page) and /about-us", "Headquarters Torrington, Connecticut -> db (hq_city, hq_state_label)", "130+ employees -> /about-us (Travis Benningfield bio)", "Certifications ISO9001, AS9100, ISO13485, IATF16949, ROHS, ITAR -> db (certifications) and /quality", "Capabilities: SMT, Through Hole, BGA, Wire & Cable, Conformal Coating, Test, Box Build, Selective Solder, Wave Solder, Leadless Device, Traceability -> /about-us and /quality", "Industries: Medical, Aerospace, Defense, Telecommunications, Industrial/Commercial, Transportation -> / (home page)", "Equipment: PVA6000, IR2000, MakerBot, ERSA Versaflow 3/66, Contact Systems CS-400, Optical Control OC Scan CCX.3, Barcode system -> db (capabilities) and / (home page blog)", "Family ownership (Steve and David Altschuler) -> / and /about-us", "AS9100 D level certified April 2017 -> / (home page)", "ITAR registered -> db (certifications)", "Prototype to production scaling -> / (home page headline)", "Integrated box build reduces hand-offs -> / (home page blog)", "Component engineering & obsolescence management -> /about-us (Andrew Zaharek bio)"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Altek Electronics offers printed circuit board assembly services to OEMs who sell products used in the telecommunications industry.", "founded_year": "1972", "employee_count": "130+", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": ["ITAR registered"], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Small business"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='altek-electronics-inc-a-cyient-dlm-company' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Earthfirst Films operates as a division of Aluf Plastics from its headquarters in Columbus, Ohio, with additional manufacturing sites in Orangeburg, New York, and Sulphur Springs, Texas. The business traces its roots to 1949 when Joe Tatem founded Plastic Suppliers as a privately held corporation in Blackwood, New Jersey. Over decades the company expanded through distribution and converting centers across the United States and Europe, beginning film manufacturing in Columbus in 1976. In 2022 the organization rebranded its biopolymer portfolio globally as Earthfirst®, and in 2025 it was acquired by API.

The Columbus campus houses two primary facilities: a blown film plant and a cast-and-tenter extrusion plant Core processes include blown film extrusion, cast and tenter extrusion, lamination, slitting, and converting. An on-site laboratory equipped with two lab extruders performs tensile, barrier, optical, FTIR, and microscopy testing. The company holds several patents on compostable sealant films and offers small-batch production with fast prototyping of laminates for brand owners.

Products target food, beverage, medical, personal care, office, industrial, and broader consumer packaged goods segments. Customers range from brand owners seeking compostable sealant and barrier sealant films to converters needing flow-wrap, shrink-sleeve, and laminated structures. The portfolio includes PLA-based films, PHA-based home-compostable grades, and other biobased polymers.

The company states its mission is to create sustainable solutions through open collaboration. Its differentiation rests on over 20 years of biopolymer extrusion experience, patented blown-extrusion technology for thin-gauge films, SQF-certified food-grade production at the blown film facility, and a commitment to rapid prototyping that acts as an incubator for new packaging ideas.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','SQF Certification (Safe Quality Food)']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Blown film extrusion", "Cast and tenter extrusion", "Lamination", "Slitting", "Converting", "Laboratory testing (tensile, barrier, optical, FTIR, microscopy)", "Rapid prototyping", "Small batch production"], "industries": ["Food", "Beverage", "Medical", "Personal Care", "Office", "Industrial", "Consumer Packaged Goods (CPG)"], "materials": ["PLA (Poly Lactic Acid)", "PHA (Polyhydroxyalkanoates)", "Biobased polymers", "Polystyrene (Polyflex)"], "equipment": ["Blown film lines", "Cast and tenter extrusion lines", "Lab extruders (two)", "High-speed slitters"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Patented blown extrusion process for biopolymer films", "Small-batch production and fast prototyping of laminates", "Home compostable solutions including PHA grades", "SQF certified blown film facility for food-grade packaging", "Over 20 years of biopolymer film extrusion expertise"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters Columbus, Ohio + locations Orangeburg NY, Sulphur Springs TX -> /about-us", "Founded 1949 by Joe Tatem as Plastic Suppliers -> /about-us", "2022 rebrand to Earthfirst, 2025 API acquisition -> /about-us", "Two Columbus facilities: blown film at 2450 Marilyn Lane, cast/tenter at 2400 Marilyn Lane -> /services", "Processes: blown film extrusion, cast and tenter extrusion, lamination, slitting, converting -> /services", "Lab with two lab extruders, testing capabilities -> /services", "Patents on compostable sealant films -> /about-us, /services", "Small batch production, fast prototyping -> /about-us", "Industries: food, beverage, medical, personal care, office, industrial, CPG -> /, /about-us", "Materials: PLA, PHA, biobased polymers, polystyrene -> /about-us, /services", "Certifications: ISO 9001:2015, SQF -> /services", "Mission: sustainable solutions through open collaboration -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Earthfirst\u00ae Biopolymer Films, a division of Aluf Plastics, is a manufacturer of compostable sealant and barrier sealant films", "founded_year": "1949", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='aluf-plastics' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Amark Wire, based in Fairfield, New Jersey, has spent over 50 years as a custom manufacturer of wires, pins, and cables. The company focuses on smaller, more difficult products that serve a wide range of industries and critical applications.

The shop specializes in drawing, grinding, straightening, cutting, forming, and spooling small-diameter wire rod from 0.002″ to 0.250″ in diameter and up to 12 feet in length. Its process lineup includes Escomatic Swiss screw machining, four-slide machining, centerless grinding, wire EDM, flattening, heading, precision bending, sand blasting, tumbling, upsetting, wire threading, cold forming, and spooling. Output ranges from conductors and drawn wire to electrical pins, electrodes, eyelets, hermetically sealed pins, guide wires, hinge pins, inserts, micro welding wire, rods, shafts, springs, step pins, studs, stylets, thermocouple wire, and tubing. All materials and products are manufactured in the United States, and the company works with a broad palette of metals including rare precious alloys.

Amark Wire serves automotive, aerospace, defense, dental, earth sciences, electrical, environmental sciences, fiber optics, glass sealing, and medical sectors. Defense and medical applications are highlighted as key markets.

The company emphasizes fast turnaround times, competitive pricing, and the ability to work with any material, including rare precious metals. It maintains original material certifications and test reports on file, offers sample parts, and treats customer schematics as confidential.', certifications=ARRAY['ROHS']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Wire drawing", "Centerless grinding", "Wire straightening and cutting", "Wire forming", "Spooling", "Escomatic Swiss screw machining", "Four-slide machining", "Wire EDM", "Flattening", "Heading", "Precision bending", "Sand blasting", "Tumbling", "Upsetting", "Wire threading", "Cold forming"], "industries": ["Automotive", "Aerospace", "Defense Applications", "Dental", "Earth Sciences", "Electrical", "Environmental Sciences", "Fiber Optics", "Glass Sealing", "Medical"], "materials": ["52 Alloy", "Alumel", "Aluminum", "Beryllium", "Brass", "Bronze", "Buss bar", "Copper", "Gold", "Hastalloy B", "Inconel", "Kovar", "Molybdenum", "Mone", "Music wire", "Nichrome", "Nickel", "Nickel silver", "Niromet 426", "Phosphorus", "Platinum", "RA 330", "Solder wire", "Tinned", "Titanium", "Tungsten", "Welding wire", "Zinc"], "equipment": ["Escomatic Swiss screw machines", "Four-slide machines", "Wire EDM machines", "Centerless grinders"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "Diameters 0.002\u2033\u20130.250\u2033 with close tolerances", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Location: Fairfield, New Jersey -> db", "Over 50 years in business -> /", "Custom manufacturing of wires, pins, and cables -> /", "Specializes in smaller, more difficult products -> /", "Processes: drawing, grinding, straightening, cutting, forming, spooling -> /services", "Diameter range 0.002\u2033 to 0.250\u2033, lengths up to 12 feet -> /services", "Escomatic Swiss Screw Machining -> /services, db", "Four Slide Machining -> /services, db", "Centerless Grinding, Wire EDM, Flattening, Heading, Precision Bends, Sand Blasting, Tumbling, Upsetting, Wire Threading, Wire