UPDATE companies SET description='American Alloy Fabrication, Inc. (AAFI) was founded in 1980 in Huntsville, Alabama, as a one-man shop offering precision welding services to local industries. The company incorporated in 1987 and moved into its current facility, which has since been expanded multiple times to accommodate growth.

Today AAFI operates as a full-service, vertically integrated contract manufacturer producing fabricated parts, industrial enclosures, custom weldments, and mechanical assemblies. Its capabilities span laser cutting, CNC turret punching, CNC forming, CNC and manual machining, robotic and manual welding (MIG, TIG, spot), metal finishing, deburring, polishing, mechanical assembly, and packaging and logistics support. The facility is equipped with advanced inspection tools including coordinate measuring machines, optical comparators, and laser scanners, and the company emphasizes design-for-manufacturability support, prototype development, and production manufacturing.

The customer base extends across diverse industries, beginning with a local engine manufacturer in the 1980s that commissioned reusable shipping racks. That project launched AAFI into large-scale contract manufacturing, and the company now serves a range of industrial sectors requiring precision metal fabrication.

AAFI differentiates itself through a quality management system that consistently achieves above 95% acceptance and on-time delivery ratings, a commitment to continuous improvement, and a partnership model that aims to function as an extension of the customer’s organization. The company states its focus on precision, high-tolerance products and long-term relationships as core to its approach.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Complete Project Management", "Design for Manufacturability (DFM)", "Prototype Development", "Production Manufacturing", "Laser Cutting", "CNC Turret Punching", "CNC Forming", "CNC & Manual Machining", "Welding (MIG, TIG, Spot, Robotic)", "Metal Finishing", "Deburring", "Polishing", "Mechanical Assembly", "Packaging, Crating and Logistics Support"], "industries": ["Engine manufacturing"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Coordinate measuring machines", "Optical comparators", "Laser scanners"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Quality acceptance and delivery performance rating consistently above 95%", "State-of-the-art inspection equipment including coordinate measuring machines, optical comparators, and laser scanners", "Vertically integrated contract manufacturing from design support through complete mechanical assembly", "Focus on precision, high-tolerance products", "Long-term partnership model acting as an extension of the customer\u2019s organization"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1980 as a one-man precision welding shop -> /about-us", "Incorporated in 1987 and moved to current facility -> /about-us", "Headquarters in Huntsville, Alabama -> db", "Capabilities: laser cutting, CNC turret punching, CNC forming, CNC & manual machining, welding (MIG, TIG, spot, robotic), metal finishing, deburring, polishing, mechanical assembly, packaging/crating/logistics, design for manufacturability, prototype development, production manufacturing, complete project management -> /", "Quality acceptance and delivery performance rating consistently above 95% -> /quality", "Inspection equipment includes coordinate measuring machines, optical comparators, laser scanners -> /quality", "Initial customer was a local engine manufacturer -> /about-us", "Focus on precision, high-tolerance products -> /about-us", "Goal to develop long-term relationships and act as manufacturing partner -> /about-us", "Vertically integrated contract manufacturer -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Today AAFI is a full service, vertically integrated contract manufacturer supplying customers with fabricated parts, industrial enclosures, custom weldments and mechanical assemblies.", "founded_year": "1980", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='american-alloy-fabrication-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='American Auto Parts operates from a 100,000-square-foot facility on five acres in Omaha, Nebraska. The company has served the greater Omaha area for over 50 years, though a precise founding year is not publicly stated.

The company supplies domestic and foreign used, remanufactured, aftermarket, and new OEM surplus auto parts. Its inventory spans engines, transmissions, car doors, radiators, differentials, transfer cases, tires, and wheels. The facility’s extensive space supports a large on-hand inventory.

Customers include fellow automotive recyclers, independent garages, body shops, and individual vehicle owners. The company ships used and remanufactured parts to any destination in the continental United States, serving both trade and retail buyers.

