UPDATE companies SET description='American Bean is headquartered in Petersburg, North Dakota, with additional facilities in Angus and Oslo, Minnesota, and Sharon, North Dakota. The company does not publicly disclose its founding year, ownership structure, or the names of its founders.

The company specializes in producing and supplying dry bean certified seed, with a portfolio that includes pinto and cranberry varieties. It works with a network of growers who adhere to rigorous production standards, and it manages seed selection, conditioning, and packaging. American Bean also operates a food safety program that has been audited and certified under the Primus GFS standard, a Global Food Safety Initiative benchmark.

Its customers include both growers who produce seed under contract and buyers worldwide who source certified dry bean seed for commercial production. The company serves the agricultural seed sector and the broader food processing industry, providing crop price information and recipes alongside its seed products.

American Bean was founded on the principle that quality products lead to increased yields and higher profitability for growers and buyers alike. It emphasizes a farm-to-fork quality standard and highlights its Primus GFS certification as evidence of its commitment to safe, superior food products.', certifications=ARRAY['HACCP','Primus GFS']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Certified dry bean seed production", "Seed selection and conditioning", "Packaging", "Food safety auditing (Primus GFS)", "Crop price information"], "industries": [], "materials": ["Dry beans", "Pinto beans", "Cranberry beans", "Certified seed"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Quality products linked to increased yields and profitability", "Farm-to-fork quality standard across all process steps", "Primus GFS certified food safety program", "Wide variety of certified dry bean seeds (pinto, cranberry, others)", "Grower network held to rigorous production standards"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Petersburg, ND; additional locations in Angus, MN; Oslo, MN; Sharon, ND -> /", "Produces dry bean certified seed, including pinto and cranberry varieties -> /", "Operates a Primus GFS certified food safety program -> /", "HACCP certification -> db", "Serves growers and buyers globally -> /", "Founded on principle that quality products mean increased yields and profitability -> /", "Company type: Manufacturer (produces seeds) -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Our growers are dedicated to exceeding our rigorous standards to produce the highest quality dry bean certified seed on the market.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='american-bean' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='American Electric Company, LLC has been headquartered in Mililani, Hawaii since its founding in 1946. The company began as an electrical contractor serving the islands and has grown into a multi-service provider with over seven decades of experience.

The firm provides electrical construction, service, controls, telecom, and alternative energy solutions. Its construction division offers design/build services using BIM modeling, TotalStation, Revit, and prefabrication, as well as high-voltage system design, installation, and testing for power plants, manufacturing facilities, and data centers. As a TEGG® Service Contractor, it delivers guaranteed service programs, ultrasonic testing, and de-energized maintenance. The service team handles emergency repairs, installations, modifications, and diagnostic power quality work.

Customers span residential homeowners, commercial property managers, industrial contractors, and utility-scale operators. The company has served alternative energy projects, power generation plants, manufacturing facilities, and data centers across Hawaii.

