l-manufacturing-co-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Applied Molding Technologies, LLC was founded in 2006 in Frederic, Wisconsin. The company began at a time when conventional wisdom held that domestic manufacturing could not compete with low-wage overseas producers, and its founders built the business on the premise that a fundamentally different operating model was required to succeed.

The shop provides thermoplastic injection molding on all-electric presses ranging from 55 to 850 tons of clamp force, and thermoset compression, transfer, and injection molding on presses from 150 to 300 tons. It also offers value-added mechanical assembly including heat-staking, ultrasonic insertion, sub-assemblies, kitting, and packaging. Production runs 24 hours a day, seven days a week, 365 days a year on a four-shift rotation designed to minimize start-up and shut-down scrap. The facility handles low- to high-volume runs and high-cavitation tooling, with new molds built domestically or off-shore and maintained in-house.

Applied Molding serves a global customer base with parts that require heat resistance, dielectric strength, and long-term stability, such as electrical and dielectric components and large or thick-section parts. As a pure custom molder with no proprietary product lines, the company scales its engineering, quality, and program-management support to each customer’s requirements, from full-scope program support to straightforward production orders.

The company was designed from first principles around three core attributes: efficiency, customization, and adaptability. Its continuous 24/7 schedule, lean headcount, and in-house core capabilities are intended to reduce fixed overhead and improve repeatability. Management emphasizes continuous improvement and structured retrospection to rebuild processes when conditions change.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Thermoplastic injection molding", "Thermoset compression molding", "Thermoset transfer molding", "Thermoset injection molding", "Mechanical assembly (heat-staking, ultrasonic insertion, sub-assemblies, kitting)", "New mold builds (single-cavity to high-cavitation)", "Off-shore tooling management", "Tool maintenance and repair", "Design for manufacturability (DFM) analysis", "Insert molding", "Automated production", "Process-controlled production", "Full traceability and documentation", "Commodity and engineering grade resin processing", "Tight-tolerance high-cavitation molding", "Electrical/dielectric component molding", "Large/thick-section part molding", "Complex geometry molding", "Repeatable fill for transfer molding", "Fast cycle time thermoset injection", "Packaging and ship-direct programs"], "industries": [], "materials": ["Commodity thermoplastic resins", "Engineering-grade thermoplastic resins", "Thermoset materials"], "equipment": ["All-electric injection presses (55\u2013850 tons)", "Thermoset presses (150\u2013300 tons)"], "volume": "Low to high volume production", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["24/7 continuous production on a four-shift rotation since inception", "Thermoplastic and thermoset molding under one roof with a single quality system", "Domestic and off-shore tooling options managed by the company", "ISO 9001:2015 certified, process-controlled quality with full traceability", "Scalable engineering and program management tailored to each program"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2006 -> /about", "Headquarters in Frederic, Wisconsin -> /", "Thermoplastic injection molding 55-850T all-electric presses -> /capabilities", "Thermoset compression, transfer, injection molding 150-300T presses -> /capabilities", "Mechanical assembly with heat-staking, ultrasonic inserts, sub-assemblies, kitting -> /capabilities", "24/7/365 production, four-shift rotation -> /about", "Domestic and off-shore tooling builds -> /", "ISO 9001:2015 certified -> /", "Pure custom molder, no proprietary products -> /about", "Scalable engineering and program management -> /about", "Continuous improvement and adaptability focus -> /about", "Serves global customers -> /", "Electrical/dielectric components and large/thick-section parts -> /capabilities", "Tool maintenance and repair -> /", "DFM analysis offered -> /products", "Insert molding capability -> /capabilities", "Automated production -> /capabilities", "Process-controlled production -> /capabilities", "Full traceability and documentation -> /capabilities", "Commodity and engineering grade resins -> /capabilities", "Tight tolerance high-cavitation work -> /capabilities", "Complex geometries and repeatable fill -> /capabilities", "Faster cycle times for thermoset injection -> /capabilities", "Packaging and ship-direct programs -> /capabilities"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Applied Molding Technologies delivers thermoplastic injection and thermoset compression, transfer and injection molding", "founded_year": "2006", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='applied-molding-technologies-llc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Applied Plastics was founded in 1976 and operates a 30,000-square-foot manufacturing facility in Portland, Oregon. The company produces machined and fabricated plastic parts from this location, serving customers across the United States, Canada, and internationally.

The shop specializes in plastic machining, acrylic fabrication, laser cutting and engraving, and cutting full sheets to size. It also extrudes UHMW board stock, including recycled UHMW, and works with a range of sheet, rod, and tube materials.

Its customer base spans the U.S., Canada, and beyond.

